---
// P8 Investors (doc 06 P8; matrix 4.4; D2): thesis + results only. C1 → C14 in order with the declared C2–C3
// compression. For impact investors only (owner, 2026-10-14). No market-size figures, valuation, raise, revenue, growth or pipeline; no partner references
// or reply-time promises (confirm list #13, #17).
// WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): the In Short summary is gone (the hero lead and the bands say it), the thesis is three cards without a lead line,
// the path-to-scale paragraph is gone (the scale FAQ answers it), three FAQs, not four. The H1 is the owner's wording.
// WP34 (cycle-11 review): the approaches comparison is gone from this page (it compared supported youth cohorts, on a page about backing the platform; Home keeps it); a short band says how
// JobReady builds on that delivery and that youth-program outcomes are not platform outcomes.
// WP36 (cycle-13 reviews): "Independent Evidence" is three sentences (the trial, the survey, the line that these are youth-program outcomes, not platform outcomes) and three links (the survey, the trial, the case
// studies); the trial explanation, the +10.3 pp chart and table and the three case-study cards are on the Impact pages. The sector taxonomy ("The Sectors Involved") is gone from the mechanism band. The platform band
// keeps its first sentence: the youth-program line now sits beside the figures it qualifies, and is said once.
// WP39 (cycle-16 review): the platform-status question points to "What JobReady Does" instead of listing the status a third time (Q11-investor), and the mechanism band carries no "Our Approach" statement (it restated the hero
// and returned to cohort language; "How JobReady Builds on Delivery" says how the platform builds on delivery).
// WP40 (cycle-17 review): "What JobReady Does" is three short cards (IncludesBand, as on every other audience page) in place of the status table, which still read as a concern / inclusion / benefit matrix. Each card states its
// status once (IN-04: partner portals and AI chat live, the employer marketplace and the gig-work marketplace in pre-launch; IN-06 and IN-08: Competent the published first level, Proficient and Expert planned,
// personalized and adaptive learning on the roadmap) and one text link goes to the full rollout status. The band keeps its id (#features): the first FAQ answer links it.
// WP42 (cycle-19 review): the track-record band (#guide) opens with the delivered figures ("Delivered Since 2014": 130,000+ learners, 150,000+ enrollments, 15 countries and territories, with their enrollment and location note), before the
// institutional relationships and the leadership; the band that held them is "Contracts, Pipeline and Recognition" (#reach: the contract scope in its own labeled block, the National University pipeline and the two badges).
// WP43 (cycle-20 review): the track-record band (#guide) is the delivered tiles, the origin line and ONE paragraph that names the institutions by type, then the link to the leadership team (it was four relationship lists and seven
// founder and leadership entries, a directory in the middle of the platform story; the link was the closing band's secondary action). The mechanism band is headed "How JobReady Connects Learning to Work" (it was "A Multi-Sided
// Model: Learn, Earn, Prosper"). The one-sentence platform band ("The Platform": "How JobReady Builds on Delivery") is gone: the evidence block above ends "Youth-program outcomes are not platform outcomes." and "What JobReady Does"
// (#features, which the first FAQ answer links) states what is live, in pre-launch and planned.
import LandingLayout from '../../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../../components/sections/HeroBand.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import CTABand from '../../../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/system/Icon.astro';
import Tone from '../../../components/pages/home/Tone.astro';
import HomeMechanism from '../../../components/pages/home/HomeMechanism.astro';
import InvestorDefinition from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorDefinition.astro';
import InvestorThesis from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorThesis.astro';
import InvestorVision from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorVision.astro';
import InvestorGuide from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorGuide.astro';
import InvestorEvidence from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorEvidence.astro';
import InvestorReach from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorReach.astro';
import InvestorFit from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorFit.astro';
import InvestorOffer from '../../../components/pages/investors/InvestorOffer.astro';
import FaqBlock from '../../../components/pages/hub/FaqBlock.astro';
import { HEADLINE, VALUE_PROPOSITION } from '../../../data/copy';
import { cta } from '../../../lib/mailto';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../../../lib/faq';
import { linkAttrs } from '../../../lib/url';
import { webPage } from '../../../lib/schema';

const path = '/partner-with-us/investors/';
const title = 'Investors';
// Meta description (≤ 155): the plan's P8 wording, a BLUF without a count. SC-01 carries a mandatory composition footnote, which a meta
// description cannot show, so the headline count stays in the page body ("Delivered Since 2014", the first tile of the track-record band, InvestorGuide) beside its note. WP38: the definition band no longer repeats it.
const description = 'For impact investors: back JobReady’s staged rollout. Request an introduction call; the deck follows under NDA.';
if (description.length > 155) throw new Error(`Investors meta description is ${description.length} characters (max 155)`);
const investor = cta('investor');
// Q11-investor (WP39, cycle-16 review): the live / pre-launch / planned list is "What JobReady Does" directly above, so the answer points there; the shared Q11 (Employers, JobReady@Work, the platform page) keeps the list.
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q11-investor', 'Q5', 'Q2-investor'];
const jsonLd = [webPage({ path, name: `${title} | CodersTrust`, description, dateModified: '2026-10-29' }), faqJsonLd('investors', path, FAQ_IDS)]; // WP108: the page states no "last updated" date; its dateModified is the day SC-02's detail was reworded

// "What JobReady Does" (WP40, cycle-17 review): three cards, one for each job the platform does for a reader of this page: learning, paid work, institutions. The status words are the register's (IN-04: "Live today: partner
// portals, marketing automation, customer relationship management and AI chat. In pre-launch: the employer marketplace and the gig-work marketplace."; IN-06: personalized and adaptive learning is roadmap;
// IN-08: "Competent is the first level; Proficient and Expert are planned"), and the two marketplaces are named as two (tests/wp25s.spec.ts). "marketplaces such as Upwork and Fiverr" keeps the old row's "such as": placement
// does not run through these two alone.
const includes = [
  {
    icon: 'graduation-cap',
    title: 'Learn Through TalentLEAP',
    // WP64 (cycle-36 review, Claude): the same sentence as the TalentLEAP page's opening, "The first published TalentLEAP level is Competent; Proficient and Expert levels are planned." (it said "Competent is the published first level; Proficient and Expert are planned.").
    text: 'The first published TalentLEAP level is Competent; Proficient and Expert levels are planned. Supported cohorts include mentoring, certification exam preparation and placement support, as agreed in the program scope.',
    facts: ['IN-06', 'IN-08', 'PD-01', 'PD-02'],
  },
  {
    icon: 'briefcase',
    title: 'Connect to Paid Work',
    text: 'The employer marketplace and the gig-work marketplace are in pre-launch. Until launch, placement runs through CodersTrust’s placement team and marketplaces such as Upwork and Fiverr.',
    facts: ['IN-04'],
  },
  {
    icon: 'building-2',
    title: 'Equip Partner Institutions',
    text: 'Partner portals and AI chat are live. Personalized and adaptive learning is on the roadmap.',
    facts: ['IN-04', 'IN-06'],
  },
];
const rollout = linkAttrs('/our-model/jobready-platform/');
const mechanismBlocks = [
  { label: 'Learn', title: 'Courses, Bootcamps and University Programs', text: 'AI-ready digital skills, with preparation for industry certification.', icon: 'graduation-cap' },
  { label: 'Earn', title: 'Jobs, Freelance Work and Gigs', text: 'Placement support and mentoring into paid work.', icon: 'briefcase' },
  { label: 'Prosper', title: 'Career Paths and Continuing Development', text: 'TalentLEAP career paths; progressive levels are planned beyond the first published level.', icon: 'trending-up' },
  { label: 'Institutions', title: 'A Digital Delivery Platform', text: 'Partner portals for governments, universities and partners.', icon: 'building-2' },
];
---

<LandingLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Partner with Us', href: '/partner-with-us/' }, { label: 'Investors' }]} stickyCta={{ label: investor.label, href: investor.href }}>
  <Tone cmf="C1">
    <HeroBand
      variant="inner"
      audience="For Impact Investors"
      title={HEADLINE.investors}
      lead={VALUE_PROPOSITION.investors}
      leadFacts={['IN-04']}
      cta={{ label: investor.label, href: investor.href }}
      artSeed="investors"
    />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="GEO"><InvestorDefinition id="definition" /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C2-C3 (compressed)"><InvestorThesis id="thesis" /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C5"><InvestorGuide id="guide" /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C4"><InvestorVision id="vision" /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C6">
    <HomeMechanism id="mechanism" tone="airy" eyebrow="The Model" title="How JobReady Connects Learning to Work" blocks={mechanismBlocks} link={{ label: 'How Our Model Works', href: '/our-model/' }} />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C7"><InvestorReach id="reach" /></Tone>
  <!-- WP36 (cycle-13 review): the evidence is three sentences and the links; the case studies are one link, "Case Studies", in the same row. -->
  <Tone cmf="C7">
    <InvestorEvidence
      id="proof-band"
      links={[
        { label: 'Impact Survey 2026', href: '/impact/outcomes-2026/' },
        { label: 'The Randomized Trial', href: '/impact/independent-evaluation/' },
        { label: 'Case Studies', href: '/impact/case-studies/' },
      ]}
    />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C8">
    <IncludesBand id="features" title="What JobReady Does" cards={includes}>
      <a slot="more" class="link" href={rollout.href}>See the Full Rollout Status<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a>
    </IncludesBand>
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C9"><FaqBlock id="faq" audience="investors" ids={FAQ_IDS} tone="ice" title="Questions Investors Ask" eyebrow="Fit and Objections"><InvestorFit /></FaqBlock></Tone>

  <!-- C10 · Differentiation: WP34 (cycle-11 review) swapped the approaches comparison for one statement ("How JobReady Builds on Delivery"); WP43 (cycle-20 review) removed that band: the evidence block above it ends "Youth-program outcomes are not platform outcomes."
       and "What JobReady Does" (the live, pre-launch and planned status) is the platform statement, so the page goes from the questions to the offer. -->

  <Tone cmf="C11"><InvestorOffer id="offer" /></Tone>

  <!-- WP43 (cycle-20 review): the "Meet the Leadership Team" link that was this band's secondary action is in the track-record band (#guide), where the leadership entries were. -->
  <Tone cmf="C13">
    <CTABand id="cta" tone="klein" heading="Let’s Talk About Backing the Platform" cta={{ label: investor.label, href: investor.href }} />
  </Tone>

</LandingLayout>
